seg-2a3a1f19005a = LEO-PNT is positioning, navigation and timing (PNT) from satellites in low Earth orbit (LEO), alongside or instead of the medium Earth orbit (MEO) global navigation satellite systems (GNSS) such as the Global Positioning System (GPS) and Galileo. This page ties together every LEO-PNT kind and scenario of the engine: what each computes, the bands and signal presets and where their numbers come from, what the navigation message carries, what is VALIDATED and what is MODELLED, and how to run each scenario. The kind pages go deeper:

