seg-f3750a8f2863 = The engine is a generic LEO-PNT simulator. Any constellation (a Walker pattern, explicit orbital elements, a two-line element set (TLE) through the Simplified General Perturbations { "4" } (SGP4) propagator, or a designed single pass), any signal design (any band, any mix of binary phase-shift keying (BPSK), binary offset carrier (BOC) and frequency-division multiple access (FDMA) components), any navigation-message model. Named systems are optional presets: data files, each with its source, which fill only what a scenario leaves out. Every capability, test, oracle and bundled scenario runs with no Celeste data present.

# text
# c1: src/celeste_iod.rs
# c2: build.rs
# c3: scenarios/*celeste-iod*.toml
# c4: tests/workshop_preset_isolation.rs
seg-4d3bd0301e59 = The Celeste IOD (in-orbit demonstration) preset is one optional preset among them. Its signal parameters were presented at the ESA NAVISP (European Space Agency Navigation Innovation and Support Programme) LEO-PNT workshop, { "2026" }, and have no public source yet. Every workshop-derived number of the engine lives in one file, <a1><c1/></a1>, which <c2/> compiles in only when it exists, and in the repository-only scenarios <c3/>. Deleting that file and those scenarios withholds the preset with no source edit; every other test, oracle and scenario runs without it (<c4/> guards which files may name it). This page gives none of its numbers.

